

    - -- 1. Short Description ]----.
- -- --- --------------------------'

    Program: RandANSI
   Function: Displays one random textfile, preferably ANSI :)
    Authors: Dreamer/Supplex/1oo% - Coding
Releasedate: Sun 25-Jun-1995 12:oo



    - -- 2. Disclaimer ]----.
- -- --- -------------------'

Use  it,  if  you like, but don't blame me for any disasters this cute prog
does  (also  it should NOT).  You may change it for your own needs, as long
as you don't change the credits and don't spread any changed version.



    - -- 3. Introduction ]----.
- -- --- ---------------------'

This little program just displays an randomly chosen Text-File when
invoked.



    - -- 4. Installation ]----.
- -- --- ---------------------'


You just have do put all Textfiles to be displayed randomly in one
directory, and name them "xxx.y" where xxx stands for one unique name,
and y for an digit ranging from 0 to 9, e.g.

Sysop-Chat.0
Sysop-Chat.1
Sysop-Chat.2
Sysop-Chat.3

Be sure y is continuously, with no missing digits!
Now just insert something like

#0Pfiles:1oo/RandANSI/RandANSI.rexx Systext:Random/SysopChat.3}
^                                                             ^
`-- CTRL-Q                                   Highest number --'

where You want to display your text randomly. Thats all...



